  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A perfectly reflecting mirror of mass <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> mounted on a spring constitutes a spring-mass system of angular frequency <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> such that <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>24</mn></mrow></msup><mtext> </mtext><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> with <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math> as Planck's constant. <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> photons of wavelength <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> strike the mirror simultaneously at normal incidence such that the mirror gets displaced by <math><mn>1</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the value of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> then the value of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is________.<br/>[Consider the spring as massless]<br ><img src=\"assets\\qt0003_8782f326df44.png\"/></p>"
  },
